<para id="RM0000005KZ013X" category="C" type-id="3008Z" name-id="5227D-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B1412/12</dtccode>
<dtcname>Ambient temperature sensor malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM0000005KZ013X_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000AIM00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The thermistor assembly (ambient temperature sensor) is installed at the front of the condenser, detects the outside air temperature and is used for "AUTO" control of the heater &amp; air conditioner. The resistance of the thermistor assembly (ambient temperature sensor) changes in accordance with changes in the outside air temperature: as the outside air temperature decreases, the resistance increases, and as the outside air temperature increases, the resistance decreases. The combination meter assembly outputs a voltage (5V) to the thermistor assembly (ambient temperature sensor), reads the voltage changes that accompany changes in its resistance, and sends a signal to the air conditioner amplifier assembly via the CAN communication line.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="left">
